Package: HEART
Type: Package
Title: Heterogeneity-Aware Empowerment via Adaptive Robust Transfer
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Haoyu", "Yang", email = "haoyuyang@hsph.harvard.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ruoyu", "Wang", role = "aut"),
    person("Xihong", "Lin", email = "xlin@hsph.harvard.edu", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Implements HEART, a procedure for target-population association
    testing (e.g. GWAS in an under-represented ancestry) that borrows strength
    from a larger, possibly heterogeneous source population. For each variant a
    target-only estimator and an auxiliary estimator (pooled, doubly robust or
    source-only) are computed, the auxiliary estimator is decorrelated from the
    target-only one through their joint sandwich covariance, and the resulting
    pair of p-values is combined through a four-group mixture model into a
    likelihood-ratio type statistic. The composite null distribution of the
    statistic is estimated from the data, giving false discovery rate and
    family-wise error rate control that is robust to source-specific signals and
    to violations of transportability.
